Priority	Project	What you should implement	Tech stack
1	Supervisor and specialist agents	Supervisor delegates requests to appropriate specialist agents.	LangGraph, OpenRouter
2	Secure MCP gateway	Authorize or reject tool calls based on agent permissions.	FastMCP, OPA, JWT
3	Agent registry and identity	Register agents with unique identities, capabilities, versions and permissions.	FastAPI, PostgreSQL, JWT
4	Secure A2A communication	Two independent agents communicate using authenticated requests.	A2A SDK, OpenRouter
5	Context budgeting and optimization	Enforce token limits, prioritize context and summarize conversation history.	LangChain, YAML
6	Centralized model gateway	Route requests across multiple LLMs with fallback mechanisms.	LiteLLM, FastAPI
7	LLM budget enforcement	Stop agent execution when token or monetary budgets are exhausted.	Redis, YAML, OpenRouter
8	DAG validation and runaway prevention	Validate LLM-generated plans, detect cycles and prevent infinite execution.	NetworkX, Pydantic
9	Least agency enforcement	Classify actions as autonomous, approval-required or prohibited.	YAML, OPA, OpenRouter
10	Permission-aware multi-tenant RAG	Retrieve documents without leaking information across tenants.	FAISS, PostgreSQL, OPA
11	Idempotent tool execution	Prevent duplicate transactions during retries.	PostgreSQL, FastAPI
12	Durable execution and recovery	Resume an interrupted agent workflow from its last checkpoint.	LangGraph, PostgreSQL
13	Golden dataset and CI/CD evaluation	Prevent deployment when agent quality falls below defined thresholds.	pytest, DeepEval, GitHub Actions
14	Distributed agent observability	Trace agent delegation, LLM calls, tool execution, latency and costs.	OpenTelemetry, Phoenix
15	Tool-calling drift detection	Detect incorrect tool selection following model or prompt changes.	OpenRouter, pytest

What should you be able to demonstrate?
Project	Critical interview scenario
Supervisor agent	What if a specialist agent becomes unavailable?
MCP gateway	What if an agent invokes an unauthorized tool?
Agent registry	How do you manage multiple agent versions?
A2A	How do you prevent unauthorized agent delegation?
Context budgeting	What if conversation history exceeds the context window?
Model gateway	What if the primary LLM provider goes down?
Budget enforcement	What if an agent consumes $100 unexpectedly?
DAG validation	What if two agents continuously call each other?
Least agency	What if an agent initiates a financial transaction?
Multi-tenant RAG	What if tenant A retrieves tenant B's documents?
Idempotency	What if a payment succeeds but the tool times out?
Durable execution	What if the orchestrator crashes midway?
Evaluation	What if a new model reduces response accuracy?
Observability	How do you identify the root cause of high p99 latency?
Tool drift	What if a model starts selecting the wrong tools?
